# Understand-Anything analysis output. NIST SP 800-53 Rev.5 SI-12 (Information
# Handling and Retention): derived analysis artifacts are local state, not
# source. Committing them leaks internal design detail from private code and —
# because the graph is the file-content allow-list and config.json gates the
# auto-update hooks — turns repository data into a security-relevant input.
# Both the current (.ua) and legacy (.understand-anything) directory names.
.understand-anything
.ua/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
coverage/
benchmark-results/
*.log
__pycache__/
.claude/
.worktrees/
homepage/public/demo/
.private/
.venv/
venv/
*.pyc
*.pyo
Thumbs.db
*.tgz
# Node.js compile cache (build artifact, never source)
node-compile-cache/
